title: Keyboard navigation
tags: Keybindings
kind: reference
aliases: keyboard default-keys
summary: The shipped keys, by family: a few single keys for what is done all the time, then a first letter for a domain and a second for a verb.

Every command can be run from the keyboard: through
<<key "command-input:focus command" "x">> and its name if nothing else, and most
often through a key of its own. Why the keys are where they are is told in
[[Choosing keybindings]]; this note lists them. <<key "help:key" "h k">> then a key
says what it runs ([[In-app help]]).

!! A key alone

|!Key |!Does |
|<<key "command-input:focus command" "x">> (or `:`), <<key "command-input:focus bash" "Shift+x">> (or `!`) |the command input, for a command or a bash line ([[The command input]]) |
|<<key "panel:focus next" "o">> |the other panel |
|<<key "panel:focus cycle" "F6">> |the left panel, the right one, then a script's question ([[Script sessions]]) |
|<<key "cursor:find self select" "f">> (or `/`), <<key "cursor:find self walk" "Shift+f">> |jump to a row by its name, or walk down into it ([[Jumping to an entry]]); in the list, its finder |
|<<key "workspace:goto 1" "1">> … `9` |a workspace |
|`=`, `-`, `0` |zoom in, out, back ([[Panel slots and layout]]) |
|Space |toggle in place: check a row, play or pause a media or a GIF |
|Enter, Shift+Enter |open the row beside, in the viewer or the detail panel ([[Opening a row]]) |
|<<key "item:delete" "Delete">> |delete the item: its file to the trash with its metarecord, else the metarecord ([[Deleting an item]]) |
|<<key "metarecord:delete" "Shift+Delete">> |delete the metarecord alone |
|↑ ↓, Home End |move the cursor ([[Generic panel commands]]) |
|← or Backspace, → |up a level, into the row |
|F1 |the help cursor ([[In-app help]]) |
|F2 |rename the file |
|F3, F4 |record a macro, run it ([[Macros]]) |
|F5 |read the panel again |
|F11, F12 |full screen, the developer tools |

!! The keys of every program

|!Key |!Does |
|Ctrl+z, Ctrl+Shift+z or Ctrl+y |undo, redo ([[The undo selection]]) |
|Ctrl+c, Ctrl+x, Ctrl+v |copy, cut, paste files (also `c c`, `c x`, `c v`) |
|Ctrl+a, Ctrl+Shift+a |check every row, none (while typing: the start of the line) |
|Ctrl+f |find in the panel ([[Find in a panel]]) |
|Ctrl+r |read the panel again (while typing: the input history) |
|Ctrl+t, Ctrl+w, Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Shift+Tab |new workspace, close it, next, previous |
|Ctrl+s, Ctrl+o, Ctrl+d |save the workspace, open a saved one, duplicate it |
|Ctrl+n |a new metarecord, node or file, in the panel that makes one |
|Ctrl+q |quit |

!! A first letter, then a verb

A letter alone that is not above starts a ''domain''; the second letter is a
''verb'', the same in every domain ([[Choosing keybindings]]):

|!Verb |!Means | |!Verb |!Means |
|`a` |add | |`d` |delete |
|`s` |set | |`c` |create |
|`r` |remove a value | |`q` |query |
|`u` |unset, empty | |`o` |open |
|`e` |edit (Shift: from empty) | |`l` |list |
|`n` |rename | |`p` |run, play |
|`t` |retype | |`z` |revert |

|!Domain |!Holds |
|`m` |the selected metarecord: `m s`, `m a`, `m r`, `m u`, `m e`, `m n`, `m t` its fields, `m d` delete it, `m i` number a folder ([[Editing metarecords in the GUI]]) |
|Shift+m or `m m`, `m q` |the same verbs on the checked metarecords, on what the list's query matches |
|`e` |the items: `e d` delete; Shift+e or `e e`, `e q` the checked ones, the query's (`E p` plays them: [[Slideshow]]) |
|`,` |tags: `, a`, `, r`, `, q`; `, -` and `, =` before them for the negative and mixed tags ([[Hierarchical tags]]) |
|`p` |the focused panel's actions: its fields (`p e`, `p q`), revert in the log (`p z`), keep a duplicate (`p k`)… |
|`v` |what is shown: `v v` split, `v f` full screen, `v x` swap; in a panel, its view flags (`v h` hidden files, `v g` grid…) |
|`t` |a panel type: `t l` list, `t d` detail, `t f` viewer, `t m` file manager… ([[Panel types]]) |
|`g` |go to: `g r` recent, `g d` a folder, `g o` a repository, `g p` a script, `g m` the file manager, `g s` the folder as a list |
|`h` |help: `h h` a page, `h c` the cursor, `h k` a key, `h x` a command |
|`w` |workspaces: `w c` new, `w o` open a saved one, `w n` rename, `w d` delete a saved one |
|`c` |the file clipboard: `c c` copy, `c x` cut, `c v` paste, `c u` empty |

!! Where it opens

What opens something takes a ''target''. Before the key, `i` puts it here, `b`
beside — in the other slot — and `n` in a new workspace: `b t l` opens a list
beside, `n g r` a recent metarecord in a new workspace. Without one, what opens
from a row goes beside, what is picked from a list goes here.

!! While typing

A text field keeps its keys, except these: Enter confirms, Escape leaves the field,
Ctrl+u empties it, Ctrl+a and Ctrl+e go to the start and the end, Ctrl+k clears to
the end, Ctrl+, and Ctrl+- walk the completion views ([[Completion views]]), Ctrl+l
clears the status bar, Ctrl+f finds, Ctrl+q quits, F1 is the help cursor.
